volved because the thing about kids is  that they require a lot of work and a  lot of sacrifice and yet they will never  be grateful that's the thing about kids  they will never ever be great yes you  teach them to say please and thank you  but they will simply never understand as  long as they are children they will  never understand what you do for them  how hard you work for them how many  sacrifices you make for them they will  never understand the anxiety and the  heartbreak and the worry and the stress  and everything they will dig they can't  they they're not capable of  understanding it they won't understand  it and that is actually part of what  parents do part of the burden we carry  for our kids is that is that we you know  we shoulder these burdens so that our  kids can just skip merrily through life  not realizing that really any of it is  happening and that's and that's what  being a kid is all of us that's what  being a kid is supposed to be about and  they're just so they they can't be  really grateful for us because they  don't understand what we do and they're  not gonna understand it until years down  the line when they have kids of their  own and then they realize that oh yeah  right so parents especially mothers I'll  say get used to expending all of this  energy doing so much for their kids and  with very little appreciation and and  that's why it's even more important once  kids are on the scene for spouses to  appreciate each other and you know I'll  say in my situation my wife stays at  home with the kids and I know  I have to make sure that my wife knows  that I appreciate what she does because  it's hard work being a mom it's  emotionally draining it's physically  taxing and and aside from my wife might  you know aside from my wife herself I'm  the only other person in the family  capable of understanding what she does  and the burden she carries and therefore  being truly grateful for what for it the  kids aren't gonna understand it the dog  and the cat are gonna stay so I'm the  only other one that can so that's why  it's so important for me to be grateful  though I know that I still could stand  to improve quite a bit in the gratitude  department or at least in the expressed  gratitude Department I'm always  eternally grateful for my wife but part  of my job as a husband and father is to  express that gratitude to show it even  more importantly and to communicate it  in somehow and it's also of course  important for husbands to be appreciated  too fortunately I do feel appreciated in  my family but my wife does communicator  appreciation but but I know that there  are there are there are many families  where that's not the case I talk to men  who feel talking men all the time who  feel like they go to work they slave  away and a thankless job to provide for  their families they come home and  they're immediately thrust back into the  father role which is okay that that's  how it goes right but they get very few  breaks they get little rest they always  have the weight of providing and  protecting on their minds on their  shoulders weighing on their souls and  yet and yet you know some men feel that  their wives take all of that completely  for granted never express any gratitude  never appear to appreciate any of it  that's how some men feel and this again  is deadly for a marriage the wives of  those men they don't realize what  they're doing to their marriage and what  they're doing to their husband they  don't realize that their marriage is on  life support because their lack of  warmth in their lack of affection and  their lack of gratitude has turned their  husbands into shells  and there are plenty of husbands who  don't realize the same about their wives  I also think that that this is what you  know when we talk about this destroying  a marriage one of the ways that this  destroys a marriage is that this can be  a contributor to adultery though of  course again so you know someone someone  commits adultery that the blame for that  is entirely on them there's never an  excuse for that but but the reality is  we're human beings and you know we have  we have there are there are always  motivations and reasons behind our  actions so someone who commits adultery  there's always gonna be some some some  things contributing to it and motivating  it and I think a lack of gratitude can  can be a big contributor to that because  I could tell you I tell you what happens  like for the case of a man doesn't feel  appreciated it doesn't feel like his  wife really cares it doesn't feel the  affection the warmth from his wife and  you know he's got that for years and  then he you know meets somebody at work  who seems to really appreciate his  skills and his talent and seems to take  him seriously and seems to take an  interest and he starts to think why  don't get this at home and then now you  have the seeds of something very very  dangerous for the marriage and I think  the exact same thing can happen for  women who don't feel appreciated and  then they meet a man who oh wow this man  notices me he seems to appreciate my  presence in my existence and all of that  so gratitude is very important and it  let me just say one more thing about  marriage because I don't want I don't  want to wrap this up without saying this  I think it's important that you know I  love I love being married  I think being married is great I really  enjoy it I I have been single and lived  by myself and I've been married I was  single there by myself for five years  married for seven so you know so far  kind of an even sort of even between the  two I can and I can weigh them and I can  say I so much prefer  being married over that so much prefer  and I just think it's important for us  to say it's because because so often  when we talk about marriage we talk  about the challenges we say it's a lot  of work we say all the things that I  just said but I think it's important to  say these things because it's true  marriages work but I think people who  aren't married they listen to this and  they end it to them it sounds like wow  marriage sounds kind of miserable like  all it does what it's all it is is work  and sacrifice is there any joy in it and  so I just want to say yes there's a lot  of joy and it's great to be married and  I highly I recommend it to anyone I  highly recommend it there has never been  a moment I can say honestly there's  never been seven years I have not ever  for a moment wish that I was still  single I travel a lot for work I go out  and I speak around the country and so I  get I guess you could say more time to  myself than then a lot of married people  do because when I travel it just it most  the time it doesn't work to bring all  the whole family with me to go speak at  the fundraising banquets and so forth so  and and you know so I'm out of my own  I'm traveling and people will ask me say  well you know that might that must be  you must really enjoy that good time  yourself go away from the family and I  say yeah you know it's it's it's nice to  get a little time yourself at on  occasion but but no every single time  whenever I go whenever I go travel I  always wish that my family was myth with  me there's never a night that goes by  when I'm traveling where I don't think  to myself wow I wish I my family here so  I highly recommend it don't be fooled  into thinking that marriage is nothing  but but work it is work but there's a  lot of joy to be found in the work and I  think in my experience all true joy and  life comes from work so that's it that's  the end of my of my fortune cookie  reading for today have a great weekend  everybody I'll talk to you next week  Godspeed
 

